Z||000000||bcwawright||05-15-2001||10:23 AM||||I am getting confused(hehe)about the controversy about which low temp. thermo and fan switch to use....some say 160 Thermo and 176 fan switch and some say 180 Therm and 196 fan switch.....anybody got some experience with both?????<BR>Also I am going to put an aluminum rad in and wondered if anyone knew a source other than Griffin Radiator. Has anyone put a 4 core alumin rad in...is there any mod to get it to fit?<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||10:48 AM||||most normal FI cars work best with the OEM temp stat and switch. A few people go to the 180* to cut out a little on heat. I have a turbo also and they seem to run by far, much better with the 160*/176*. Mine would barely run without missing with the OEM. 180* helped but still cut out bad at high rpm. With the 160* its worked perfectly for over 3 years now. I think its been explained to me that with the turbo, an over rich mixture works best because of more airflow and the 160* makes the computer think its colder, thereby enriching the mixture. It does cut down slightly on gas milage, but whats 1 or 2 mpg.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bcwawright||05-15-2001||11:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>most normal FI cars work best with the OEM temp stat and switch. A few people go to the 180* to cut out a little on heat. I have a turbo also and they seem to run by far, much better with the 160*/176*. Mine would barely run without missing with the OEM. 180* helped but still cut out bad at high rpm. With the 160* its worked perfectly for over 3 years now. I think its been explained to me that with the turbo, an over rich mixture works best because of more airflow and the 160* makes the computer think its colder, thereby enriching the mixture. It does cut down slightly on gas milage, but whats 1 or 2 mpg.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi Roger<BR>Thanks so much for the info<BR>Which turbo are you running.....did you use an intercooler?<BR>Did you change the fuel injectors?<BR>Did you bore out the throttle body and plenum to maech throttle body bore increase??<BR>Thanks again. (nice looking car!!!!!)<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||01:47 PM||||I bought the kit uninstalled, but from an individual. It supposed to be an AirResearch. I have 3.1, but used everything, injectors, intake, comptr from orig 2.8. stock throttle body. I went to the 3.1 to gain 4 bolt main webs, forged crank a little bit more cubes. It was a special order engine out of a Z-24. Just added an accel coil, but other than that is basicly stock. Im still using orig 2.8 rad too. Never gets close to getting hot, even with AC on in traffic on a 95* day.||||reg||1
